<title>MEXICO: Banco de Mexico assigns all secondary auctions.</title>
<headline>Banco de Mexico assigns all secondary auctions.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mexico assigned all six auctions in which it sought to drain 6.601 billion pesos from the secondary market Thursday, dealers said.</p>
<p>The auctions were assigned as follows:</p>
<p>    AMOUNT     TERM     AVERAGE RATE</p>
<p>    1.100 bln  8 days   25.34 pct</p>
<p>    1.100 bln  7 days   25.18 pct</p>
<p>    1.100 bln  6 days   25.14 pct</p>
<p>    1.100 bln  5 days   24.99 pct</p>
<p>    1.100 bln  4 days   24.90 pct</p>
<p>    1.101 bln  1 day    24.88 pct</p>
<p>*Amounts in pesos</p>
<p>(( --Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559))</p>
